  "actionItems": [
    "Prioritize back volume next period by adding at least 2 to 3 sets of rowing movements, such as barbell rows or cable rows, to reverse the dip in the back strength index from 101 to 96 and address the push-to-pull imbalance.",
    "Maintain or slightly increase chest training intensity rather than volume, since your chest strength index is already climbing well. Focus on progressive overload on the bench press itself, aiming to add small increments of weight or reps compared to this period.",
    "Add 1 to 2 sets of biceps work alongside your back sessions to bring the biceps volume up from its current floor of 2 sets, which will support elbow joint health and improve your overall push-pull balance.",
    "Keep shoulder volume steady at its current 4 sets but ensure the exercises used are challenging enough to drive the shoulder strength index beyond its current plateau at 104, as strong shoulders are a key secondary driver of a heavy bench press."
  ],
  "contextSummary": "Excellent chest and triceps strength gains this period (chest index 106 to 112, triceps 105 to 108) directly support the 100 kg bench press goal, but back strength dipped (101 to 96) and the push-to-pull volume ratio is skewed at roughly 41% chest vs 19% back — rebalancing pulling work is the main priority next period."
}
